From: justririll (x1e-sleep)
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa: make DRIPS system-sleep-only

From https://github.com/justririll/x1e-sleep (kernel/sleep/dts-hamoa-add-ss1-idle-state.patch), without
the SS1 runtime state: on X1E at EL2, SS1 (0x02000154) in power-domain-system
hangs the SoC once the ADSP is attached (Surface Pro 11 findings,
https://github.com/ramonjesusmiranda-debug/sp11-el2), and on this T14s it was rejected at every runtime attempt.
Keep DRIPS (domain_ss3) for system sleep only; from runtime idle it hangs
the SoC after the first s2idle.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index 20f772235d76..6a4c704f58dd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -311,6 +311,8 @@ domain_ss3: domain-sleep-0 {
 				entry-latency-us = <2500>;
 				exit-latency-us = <2500>;
 				min-residency-us = <9000>;
+				/* DRIPS from runtime idle hangs the SoC after the first s2idle */
+				system-sleep-only;
 			};
 		};
 	};
